# ==============================================================================
# Database: L4 p0f v3 TCP SYN Operating System Signatures
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Field Schema:
#   TTL Tier (32/64/128/255) | TCP Options Layout | WScale | Win | OS Name | Score (1-99) | Device Type | Vendor
#
# Rules for Adding Entries:
#   1. Strict Specificity Order:
#      a. Exact WScale & Exact Window Size (e.g. 8|64240)
#      b. Exact WScale OR Exact Window Size (e.g. 8|* or *|8192)
#      c. Options layout matches (e.g. ^mss,nop,ws,sok,ts|*|*)
#      d. Fallbacks with wildcards (*|*|*) ALWAYS at the very bottom of each TTL block.
#   2. Printer patterns MUST precede gaming consoles to avoid false matches.
#   3. TCP option regexes accept both canonical tokens (mss/ws/sok/ts/nop)
#      and Argos sniffer shorthand (M1460/W10/S/T/N). This keeps the OpenWrt
#      and distributed Docker classifiers on the same signature contract.
#   4. WScale-only Linux/Android overlaps are context, not high-confidence
#      device identities. Exact window combinations remain identity evidence.
#
# Example:
#   128|^[Mm][Ss0-9]*,[Nn][OoPp]*,[Ww][Ss0-9]*,[Nn][OoPp]*,[Nn][OoPp]*,[Tt][Ss]*,[Ss][OoKk]*|8|64240|Windows|94|pc|Microsoft
#   64|^[Mm][Ss0-9]*,[Ss][OoKk]*,[Tt][Ss]*,[Nn][OoPp]*,[Ww][Ss0-9]*|10|65535|Android|94|smartphone|Android
# ==============================================================================

# ==============================================================================
# Windows NT Kernel Family (TTL 128)
# ==============================================================================
# 1. Exact WS & Exact Window Size
